%I A400454 #31 Sep 28 2026 15:35:29
%S A400454 1,2,3,5,6,10,11,14,16,18,22,26,34,62,107,135,136,270,271,318,371,456,
%T A400454 573,646,685,958,1358,1583,1637,2071,2746,3312,3983,4243,4431,4472,
%U A400454 7662,11051,13895,16224
%N A400454 Numbers k such that (2^k-1)*2^(k+3)+1 is a prime.
%C A400454 Largest primes have been shown prime using the Lucas-Lehmer-Riesel test (see Wright link).
%C A400454 Let N = N(k) = (2^k-1)*2^(k+3)+1, and M = A000225(k+1) = 2^(k+1)-1.
%C A400454 Conjecture: If 2^((N-1)/4) == -1 (mod N), then N is prime.
%H A400454 Gary Wright, <a href="https://mathrelated.co.uk/index.php/2026/09/04/element-2-and-set-1-12tx2t3/">Element 2 and set 1+(-1+2^t)×(2^(t+3))</a>, Sep 04 2026.
%H A400454 Gary Wright, <a href="https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/5148637/new-prime-test-for-proth-numbers">New prime test for Proth numbers</a>, Mathematics StackExchange, Sep 04 2026.
%o A400454 (Python)
%o A400454 n=lambda k: (1<<k)-1 << k+3 | 1
%o A400454 is_A400454=lambda k: (x:=pow(4,2**k,N:=n(k))) + pow(x,2**k,N) == N
%o A400454 for k in range(1000):
%o A400454     if is_A400454(k): print(k)
%Y A400454 Cf. A000225.
%K A400454 nonn,more,new
%O A400454 1,2
%A A400454 _Gary Wright_, Sep 26 2026
